I just tried the patchlevel 6 code and I like it.  The very first (and only)
game I played I got to level 6 (before going back to level 2 to die by a
bag of tricks).  I see that the initial player stats are more competitive
now.

Corpses seem to appear a lot less, and what was weird was that my little
dog preferred starving to eating anything off the ground.  I let her
have a chance at jackal meat, orc meat, and rat meat but she passed it
up.  She didn't even eat dead kitten or dead giant bat which has been
a favorite pet staple from long ago.

One comment on the door code.  I like seeing the difference between
open/closed and no doors.  But it is weird that you can move diagonally
from no door but can't from a door.  Especially since you can open and
close doors diagonally.

Finally, I was shopping for code at (I think) ohio state a few months ago
and found patches to be applied to Eric Raymond's hack font for UNIX PC.
Has this been kept current, does anyone else have it?  The thought of
graphics characters instead of letters is quite appealing.
